            <ArticleTitle>Association between breast-feeding and severity of acute viral respiratory tract infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>986-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/INF.0000000000000364</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a cross-sectional analysis of 629 mother-infants dyads, breast-feeding (ever vs. never) was associated with decreased relative odds of a lower versus upper respiratory tract infection (adjusted odds ratio: 0.64; 95% confidence interval: 0.42-0.99). There was not a significant association between breast-feeding and bronchiolitis severity score or length of hospital stay.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
